{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\n`docs/event-schema.md` presents retired shell files as current writers and omits recognized event categories from its main contract. Ticket barky-suit-dial began the accepted documentation truth sweep but left historical shell names in the current table. F05 remains deferred, so this task must not add a generated catalog or parity gate.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Replace retired writer names with maintained producer seams.\n- Add `KEY_ADD` and `KEY_REVOKE` to the replayed event inventory.\n- Separate reducer-ignored sidecars from replay mutations.\n- Classify `PRECONDITIONS` and `SYNC` as recognized non-replay records.\n- Name the direct `BRIDGE_ALERT` producer.\n- Remove the deleted-writer footnote while preserving sidecar and compatibility semantics.\n- Run focused event-schema contracts and documentation checks.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Every current writer entry names a maintained producer seam.\n- [x] Replayed event types include `KEY_ADD` and `KEY_REVOKE`.\n- [x] Reducer-ignored sidecars are distinct from replay mutations.\n- [x] `PRECONDITIONS` and `SYNC` are classified as recognized non-replay records.\n- [x] The direct `BRIDGE_ALERT` producer is named.\n- [x] The deleted-writer footnote is absent.\n- [x] No generated catalog or parity gate is added.\n- [x] Focused event-schema and documentation checks pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787534348337615001,"uuid":"59047d91-06ee-45c5-8652-b80956a4fd29"}